        return super().format(record)\n```\n\nWait, but base format will call record.getMessage() -> msg % args. If we set record.msg = truncated and args = None, then getMessage returns truncated. But we must ensure we use shallow copy rather than mutate original. Need `import copy`. But `copy.copy` on LogRecord: LogRecord has `__dict__`, and also special attributes. copy.copy works for normal objects via __reduce_ex__; LogRecord has no __copy__; copy.copy creates new instance of the class without calling __init__ and copies __dict__. Should work. Better use `copy.copy`.\n\nActually careful: after shallow copy, record.message set to truncated, msg=truncated, args=None. But exc_info and stack_info preserved. Then super().format(record) appends exception text and stack info after the truncated message — requirement says budget excludes exception traceback and stack_info, which matches since we truncate only message and base format appends the rest. Good.\n\nBut one subtlety: the truncation must count after substitution. Yes getMessage.\n\nAlternatively, we can avoid copy by computing directly and calling formatMessage. But copy is simpler and safe.\n\nHowever, `_truncate_message`: budget breakdown. If len(message) <= budget, return as-is. Else marker = \"...<omitted>...\" (len 15). remaining = budget - 15. head = ceil(remaining/2) = (remaining + 1)//2; tail = remaining - head. Result = message[:head] + marker + (message[-tail:] if tail else \"\"). For budget 32: remaining = 17; head = 9; tail = 8. Matches example. Good. Note if budget stays >=32, remaining >=17 so head>=9, tail>=8, always positive.\n\nEdge: if message shorter than head+tail but longer than budget? Can that compound? If len(message) > budget = head+tail+15, then len > head+tail+15 > head+tail, so slicing head and tail don't overlap. Good.\n\nNow \"先完成 %s 等参数替换，再计算消息长度\" and multi-line prefix continues to use record.message. In the format method after calling super().format(record) we use `record.message`. Since super().format sets record.message = record.getMessage() on our copy — same truncated message. Good.\n\nDefault init: `_setup_logger` should pass `max_message_chars=envs.DEEPINFER_LOG_MAX_MESSAGE_CHARS`. Need import: `from deepinfer.environ import envs`. Check for circular imports: environ.py imports? Let's check environ.py imports (os, threading, timedelta, Callable). It likely doesn't import logger. So logging module importing environ is safe. But logger.py is imported early... Let me check whether environ imports logger somewhere. The full file was read earlier of environ lines 1-30 maybe. Let's read environ.py first lines to confirm imports.\n\n3. stats_logger.py: change `logger.info(m)` to `logger.info(m, extra={\"keep_full_message\": True})`.\n\nNeed to confirm the logger call only there. Let's inspect the exact snippet.\n\nAlso need to ensure `_setup_logger` called at import, env read. That works.\n\nAlso requirement 6: \"重复初始化不能重复添加处理器\" — existing code already handles. `_setup_logger` recreates formatter each time using current cached config value. Old formatters on existing handlers? _default_handler is reused and its formatter replaced — meaning old formatter replaced, but spec says \"已创建的旧格式化器保留原预算\" — that refers to independently created formatter instances retaining their own max. Replacing the default handler's formatter with a new one using new cached config is what's asked: \"重新执行默认日志初始化时，将当时的配置值应用到新的格式化器\". Fine.\n\nAlso requirement: type check bool not int. In __init__:\n```python\nif max_message_chars is not None:\n    if isinstance(max_message_chars, bool) or not isinstance(max_message_chars, int):\n        raise ValueError(f\"max_message_chars must be None or an int >= 32, got {max_message_chars!r}\")\n    if max_message_chars < 32:\n        raise ValueError(...)\n```\n\nTests earlier failed with \"test_invalid_budget[64] - TypeError: New...\" hmm, maybe test expects keyword-only. Baseline 50 failed 10 passed.\n\nNow let me first rea